HHIISSTTOORRYY
       John Walker wrote ppggmmccrraatteerr in 1991 and it  was  included  in  Pbmplus.
       ppggmmccrraatteerr did the equivalent of pamcrater | pamshadedrelief.  In Netpbm
       10.68 (September 2014), Bryan Henderson split  the  functions  of  ppggmm‐‐
       ccrraatteerr  into  two  programs, one (ppaammccrraatteerr) to compute elevations, and
       the other (ppaammsshhaaddeeddrreelliieeff) to generate a shaded  relief  visual  image
       showing those elevations.  Bryan did this because it is more in keeping
       with Netpbm's modular architecture,  and  because  the  ppaammsshhaaddeeddrreelliieeff
       might be useful with other inputs.

       (Like  all  Netpbm  programs,  ppggmmccrraatteerr was not static between the two
       events described above; minor changes, including replacement of most of
       the code, happened in between).

